WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.520
The eastern lands of Europe are a vast flat
area called the European plain.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.340
It’s intersected with large waterways, thick
forests and flush meadows.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.940
Such geography meant that throughout History
this land had extensive natural resources

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.830
that could be used for farming, fishing, hunting,
etc. supporting a large population.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:24.480
However the flat lands also paved the way
for an ease of access to many migrating groups.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.360
And such was the early history for most of
eastern Europe, with many tribes coming and

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.940
going but in the grand scheme of things still
leaving this vast land largely unpopulated.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.110
However one people group that would change
this where the eastern slavs.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:42.110
They largely came in to the vast lands of
eastern europe during the 6th century slavic

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.110
migrations.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.920
Although valid arguments can be made that
some small slavic settlements may have existed

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.050
in the area for a far longer time.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.239
Nonetheless the reason why the eastern slavs
where the ones able to populate such a vast

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:56.050
area is usually attributed to two main things.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:59.739
First the sheer number of them, and how do
we know this?

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:03.719
Well even though we can’t know it for sure
because we have no written records, archeology

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:08.090
combined with the fact that their western
and southern brothers that came in to central/western

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:12.829
europe in such large numbers that even western
authors were surprised it is most likely that

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:16.409
eastern slavs did the same maybe even on a
larger scale.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:21.100
Second is the fact that eastern slavs as oppose
to the other slavs used a slash and burn farming

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.229
method mixed with hunting and gathering.

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:27.799
This combined with no crop rotation and very
rich soil and fauna of eastern europe meant

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:32.340
that they could produce a lot of food however
would have to resettle every few years due

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.350
to hunting and soil depletion.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:38.420
However these resources could in few years
replenish and be used again by a different

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.970
slavic clan resettling.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:45.020
All this meant that you had a large constantly
moving, reproducing, resettling population

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:49.349
with more than adequate food supply, which
resulted in the fact that these slavs were

00:01:49.349 --> 00:01:54.389
able to settle this vast area and become in
most regions the majority people group.

00:01:54.389 --> 00:01:58.999
Going down the mostly empty center, going
northward and meeting baltic and finno-ugric

00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:03.380
groups, and eventually also going south meeting
first the Avars, then the bulgars, then the

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.380
Khazars etc.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:09.070
In fact it is largely believed that by the
start of the 8th century most eastern slavs

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:13.090
living in the south were forced to pay some
sort of a tribute to the Khazars.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:16.980
The important thing to understand about these
eastern Slavs expanding in to the european

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:21.719
plane is that they weren’t as homogeneous
in culture and language as we may have thought.

00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:26.239
Thanks to some findings of slavic birch bark
writings in Novgorod dating back to as far

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:30.480
as the 10th century, we can tell with pretty
good certainty that there was quite a bit

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.640
of diversity between the many eastern slavic
tribes that settled the european plane.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.540
And looking at much more recent historical
eastern slavic documents or even contemporary

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:43.319
ones we can tell by comparison that the eastern
slavic cultural and language was very much

00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:46.829
convergent since the 10th century or even
earlier.

00:02:46.829 --> 00:02:47.829
But i digress.

00:02:47.829 --> 00:02:51.900
It was also around the 8th century and maybe
in some places as early as the 7th century

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.120
that the slavs slowly started to move from
the slash and burn farming method and hunting

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.560
to more reliable crop rotation farming.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.700
This meant that the chaotic autonomous nature
of constant resettling started to be replaced

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:07.150
by the creation of many small self independent
areas of farming communities.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:11.650
These communities where held together by the
main family/clan alliances that divided up

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.780
the arable and pastoral land and together
defended it from outsiders.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.400
It was in to this Slavic society that the
famous Varangians arrived around in the 8th

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.400
century.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.990
Although again arguments can be made that
norse people from Sweden may have come to

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.439
eastern europe even earlier then that but
these would only be trading expeditions.

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:33.349
However the arrival of the varangians in the
8th century was a much different story.

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:38.260
Yes some came for trade but many of them came
to plunder and settle the rich areas around

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:40.560
the vast waterways of eastern Europe.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:46.109
Side note here, the word Varangian is mostly
used to describe norse/viking “outsiders”

00:03:46.109 --> 00:03:50.530
from sweden that usually but don’t necessarily
are in one way or another connected to the

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:54.340
eastern lands of europe mostly through service
to some kind of a chieftain.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.779
With these arriving Varangians also came two
major changes.

00:03:57.779 --> 00:04:02.180
One was the increase in trade between the
Blacksee/the middle east and the Baltics and

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:06.469
that is how the scandinavians acquired the
knowledge of making damascus steel which came

00:04:06.469 --> 00:04:10.980
from India prompting the creation of the famous
viking ulfberht swords.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.379
And second was the restructuring of the eastern
european predominantly slavic society.

00:04:15.379 --> 00:04:19.150
This meant that at the beginning of the 9th
century the close knit family communities

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:23.400
that existed up until now started to make
way for the creation of large settlements

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.940
with ditches, ramparts and market places.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.870
This in turn fueled even more trade and economic
development but also the centralization of

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:34.430
power in to small chieftainses runned from
these newly created fortified towns.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:38.470
And since most of these towns were established
by incoming Varangians most of these early

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:43.460
chieftains where Varangians, ruling over a
much larger slavic population.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:47.669
However there most likely existed some small
chieftences around, that where just Slavic.

00:04:47.669 --> 00:04:52.190
It was also during this time that a new word
for the Varangians emerged, the Rus.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:56.870
Derived from a norse word to row, as many
of the Varangians would do, rowing up and

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:59.130
down the eastern european waterways.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:03.550
But it is important to note the difference
between the Rus and the Varangians, unlike

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:08.860
the Varangians the Rus mostly refered to norse
people born and living in eastern Europe including

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:09.940
the many chieftains.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:14.250
This is why foreign writers like Ahmad Ibn
Fadlan who wrote the first hand account of

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:18.770
a viking funeral referred to the Norseman
as the Rus, because they came from eastern

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.569
Europe not Scandinavia.

00:05:20.569 --> 00:05:24.970
But the word Rus later started to be used
not just for the norse people and Chieftains

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:29.470
but also their subjects, which where mostly
slavic, this combined with the fact that the

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:34.050
Rus chieftains and people overtime assimilated
in to the much larger Slavic population the

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:39.820
word Rus kind got assimilated as well, with
all eastern slavs being called the Rus by

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.990
around the 11th and 12th century.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:46.539
But going back to the 9th century from here
as it so often does some chieftenses started

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:50.139
to grow more powerful than others and absorb
the weaker ones.

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:53.970
Forming large town centers some of which we
would even recognize today.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.790
And this is where most historians start referring
to one of the most important Eastern European

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:03.289
historical documents, the nestor’s chronicle
or the primary chronicle or just Povest.

00:06:03.289 --> 00:06:07.680
Now there’s many problems with the primary
chronicle that could have it’s own entire

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.470
video like for example the fact it most likely
wasn’t even written by nestor, or that it

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:16.780
was written 2 to 3 hundred years after the
certain events it talks about, or the fact

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:21.430
that its starts of with a mistakes stating
the wrong starting date of Michael the 3rd’s

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:22.819
reign (Byzantine Emperor), etc.

00:06:22.819 --> 00:06:27.340
However, this is not to say that we should
dismiss the entire Primary Chronicle.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:32.379
Because not all of it that we can check with
archeology or other documents is wrong.

00:06:32.379 --> 00:06:33.430
Just some of it is.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:37.390
Therefore we have to be aware that the events
it talks about that we at the moment can’t

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:41.169
check with other means may be wrong or altered
from the truth.

00:06:41.169 --> 00:06:45.710
So with that in mind I will sight the primary
chronicle however also combine it with any

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:49.720
other possible sources to try to get the most
completely picture as it stands.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:50.720
So hold on to your hats as it gets a bit convoluted
from here.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.060
The primary chronicle states that the Slavic
tribes along with some Finno-Ugric tribes

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:58.669
rebelled against their Varangian overlords
and chased them out of the Lands of Eastern

00:06:58.669 --> 00:07:00.319
Europe in the early 9th century.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:04.500
Now this may be true for some chieftences
that existed at the time but eastern europe

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:09.110
wasn’t one big unified area and what may
have occurred in one of the chieftaincies

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.189
probably didn’t happen in all of them.

00:07:11.189 --> 00:07:14.789
After that it is said that the people who
through out the Varangians started to squabble

00:07:14.789 --> 00:07:17.069
amongst themselves and chaos ensued.

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:21.970
To fix this problem some of these tribes invited
back the Varangians to restore order.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:28.449
The Varangians agreed and came in 860 to 862,
with a large force lead by a person named

00:07:28.449 --> 00:07:29.449
Rurik.

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:33.590
However it is debated if Rurik really came
being invited or just came as another conqueror

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:37.560
trying to get land for himself, just like
many vikings did in western Europe.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:42.400
It is also very likely that Rurik came to
take the land from another Varangian/Rus and

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:46.629
the expulsion story never happened, being
invented years later to make it seem like

00:07:46.629 --> 00:07:50.139
a union between the Varangians and the slavs
not a conquest.

00:07:50.139 --> 00:07:55.520
There’s also a Byzantine source stating
a Rus siege of constantinople in 860 where

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:58.199
the Rus laid siege to the city before retreating.

00:07:58.199 --> 00:08:02.409
This is the same year as the early estimates
of Ruriks arrival to Eastern Europe so we

00:08:02.409 --> 00:08:03.509
know it wasn’t Rurik.

00:08:03.509 --> 00:08:07.460
It may have been a different Rus chieftain
of eastern Europe, or it may have been a independent

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:12.110
raiding expedition of some Rus people wanting
to get rich or it may have been an expedition

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:15.460
by the Chief of the northern lands that Rurik
was now conquering.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:19.120
The ladder would make some sense as Rurik
would naturally want to attack during the

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.539
absence of the Chieftain and his army.

00:08:21.539 --> 00:08:26.349
On top of that the Byzantines sources state
that the Rus suddenly lifted the seage leaving,

00:08:26.349 --> 00:08:28.370
even though they had the upper hand.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:32.690
So it may have well been the Chieftain quickly
trying to get back to his lands because Rurik

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:33.690
was there.

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:37.840
Whatever may have happened we know that Rurik
won, solidifying his reign over the northern

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:42.529
lands and supposedly founding Novgorod in
the later half of the 9th century.

00:08:42.529 --> 00:08:47.170
But this has been disproven as archeological
finds date the settlement of Veliky Novgorod

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:48.680
to late 10th century.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:54.910
However this probably was just a misinterpretation
as Novgorod just means new city or new fortification,

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:58.650
so Ruriks “new city” wasn’t the “new
city”.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:01.680
Shortly after that Rurik died in 879.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:07.100
Leaving his kingdom and a very young son Igor
to quote unquote “his kin” Oleg.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:12.060
The primary Chronicle states that Oleg went
on an expansionist campaign conquering many

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:17.330
chieftaincies and cities including Kiev in
882 which he promptly named as the capital

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:20.450
of a kingdom from then on known as the Kievan
Rus.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:25.150
He then died in 912 after which Igor, Rurik’s
son succeeded him.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:30.900
But there’s a Khazar letter from 940 mentioning
Oleg being the king of the Rus, well after

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.310
the primary chronicle states that he died.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:38.260
So this prompted some historians to think
that maybe Oleg didn’t really die in 912

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:41.960
but actually had a power struggle with Igor
well in to the 9th century.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:46.510
Whichever it may have been Igor did succeed
Oleg eventually becoming the King of the Kievan

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:47.510
Rus.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:51.900
In the 940s he went on to fight the Byzantines,
probably oversaw raiding expeditions along

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:56.480
the Caspian sea and eventually was killed
by his own subjects for demanding too many

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:59.110
tributes/taxis in 945.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:04.460
But his wife Olga took initiative and as a
regent for their young son Sviatoslav hunted

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:08.950
down the people that killed her husband, established
new frontiered castles, centralized the power

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:13.270
within the kingdom and enacted first ever
law reforms in eastern Europe.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:17.020
She was also the first high ranking person
in eastern europe to convert to Christianity

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:21.520
in Constantinople and therefor today she’s
known as Saint Olga of Kiev.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:26.650
And even though his mother was a christian
Sviatoslav was a starch pagan his entire life.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:31.380
With that said Sviatoslav fought many successful
wars against the Byzantines, the Bulgars,

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:35.900
the Khazars who were replaced by another invading
nomadic group the Pechenegs, etc.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.450
Forming at the time the largest Empire in
Europe.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:43.600
However in 970 his streak would end being
defeated by the Byzantines who then bribed

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:47.840
the Pechenegs to ambush him on his way home
from the unsuccessful campaign.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:51.650
The ambush was successful killing Sviatoslav
in 972.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.620
And since he didn’t have time to solidify
most of his conquests lots of the land he

00:10:55.620 --> 00:11:01.170
conquered was lost in the subsequent 6 year
long succession crisis between his 3 sons.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:06.450
The eldest, Yaropolk, prince of Kiev, the
second eldest, Oleg, prince of Drelinia and

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:10.450
the youngest and also a bastard, Vladimir,
prince of Novgorod.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:14.790
Yaropolk in Kiev was poised to become the
king of the Rus and as such waited to find

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:20.840
a causes belly for attacking one of his brothers
and when one dubious claim came in 977 he

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.010
seaced on the opportunity and attacked Oleg.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:26.720
Quickly conquering Drelinia and killing his
brother.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:30.870
He then turned his attention to Vladimir but
after Vladimir found out about his brothers

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:35.560
death he new that the balance of power within
the kingdom wasn’t in his favor and fled

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:38.830
leaving the Yaropolk as the sole ruler of
the Kievan Rus.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:40.290
But Vladimir had a plan in mind.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:44.900
He fled to Scandinavia to one of his relatives
Håkon Sigurdsson a vassal king of Norway

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.210
under the famous Harald Bluetooth.

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:52.470
He asked Hakon for help who did, but Vladimir
also most likely heavily recruited soldiers

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:58.430
on his own, promising land, money and seats
at his court ones they retake Kievan Rus.

00:11:58.430 --> 00:12:02.700
With this new Varangian army assembled, Vladimir
returned to Eastern Europe.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:08.140
However on his way to Kiev he stopped by Polotsk
and asked the local princess to marry him.

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:12.550
She refused to marry a bastard and so Vladimir
did the only sensible thing he could have

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:13.550
done.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:17.250
Conquered the town, killed her father and
forced her to marry him anyways.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:21.710
After that he also conquered Smolensk, after
which he could finally move on to besiege

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:27.960
Kiev, where in 978 through deceit he managed
to kill his brother Yaropolk, ending the 6

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.580
year long succession crisis.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:34.070
Vladimir went on to solidify his kingdom and
reconquer most of the lands lost since his

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:35.270
father's death.

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:39.830
But at this point Kievan Rus was a cultural
and a religious melting pot.

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:45.100
Most of the peasants practiced slavic paganism
but there were also Khazar jews, norse pagans,

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:50.290
volga bulgar muslims, finno ugric pagans,
christians, and even the nobility practiced

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:53.220
a weird mixture of norse slavic paganism.

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:56.860
All of these different religious believes
naturally didn’t provide much stability

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:57.910
to the kingdom.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:01.860
So Vladimir decided it’s time to reform
the religion of the Rus people and send out

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:05.610
envoys to go find out more about all the various
religions.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:10.430
He was put off by islams taboo on drinking
stating that “Drinking is the joy of all

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:11.430
Rus'.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:12.910
We cannot exist without that pleasure.".

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:17.200
He rejected Judaism as well as he didn’t
like the fact that they lost control of their

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.200
Holy Land.

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:23.430
And In the end he settled on Orthodox Christianity
being told their churches were much more lavish

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:26.730
and grandiose then the ones of the Catholics
in the west.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:31.790
Vladimir was baptized in 988 and set about
converting the rest of his subject effectively

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.930
closing the pages on the formerly pagan Kievan
Rus.

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:38.620
That is where I will end my early Eastern
Slavic History video.

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:41.280
